# PLAN1_SEC — file:// completion refuse

File: openOODA/audit/plan1_sec.oot
Wave 3 ATTACK. Own this note. Do not edit the worktree product files.
Do not edit dirty parent /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda.

Logline: Completion loads a file:// path, refuses `..`, calls no process_exec, and prints no file body.
Setup: Worktree /home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-lsp-complete. New path is cli/lsp_complete.oo plus the textDocument/completion branch in cli/lsp_reply.oo.
Beats:
  1. Trace the file:// load and the `..` gate.
  2. Prove the new path has no process_exec.
  3. Prove the reply and logs do not carry the loaded source.

## 0. Verdict

PASS

`..` is refused. No process_exec on the new completion path.
No file body is printed. Product was not edited.

## 1. Load path

  Dispatch (cli/lsp_reply.oo):

    method == "textDocument/completion"
      -> lsp_ok(id, lsp_complete_result(fs, body))

  Load (cli/lsp_complete.oo `lsp_comp_load`):

    1. `lsp_comp_uri` takes the first `file://` in the JSON-RPC body
       and slices until the next `"`.
    2. Empty path returns "".
    3. Path with `..` returns "".
    4. Missing or unreadable path returns "".
    5. Else `read_file(fs, p)`. Err yields "".

  Source is used only to build the prefix. The result object is a
  fixed catalog. Labels, docs, and insertText are string literals.

## 2. `..` is refused

  Gate:

    if str_index_of(p, "..") >= 0 { return ""; }

  Cases that do not call `read_file`:

    file://../etc/passwd
    file://foo/../../etc/passwd
    file://fixtures/..
    file://..
    file:///home/x/../etc/passwd
    file://foo\..\secret

  Fail-closed: a legal name that contains `..` is also refused.

  Hover loader `lsp_load_src` is loose. It has no `..` gate.
  Completion does not use that loader.

  Scratch replay of the same extract-and-gate (not product, /tmp only)
  printed `scratch_dotdot_gate: PASSED`.

  `%2e%2e` is not a `..` bypass. `oo_read_file` does not URL-decode.
  `to_cpath` rejects an embedded NUL. fopen sees the literal name.

## 3. No process_exec

  cli/lsp_complete.oo: `process_exec` appears only in a comment.
  cli/lsp_reply.oo: no `process_exec` and no `sys_exec`.
  Completion branch calls only `lsp_complete_result`.

  Pre-existing residual: cli/lsp_drive.oo still frames with `sys_exec`
  and python3. That is not this ship. This ship did not add it.

## 4. No file body printed

  `lsp_complete_result` does not `println` the source.
  It does not `write_file` the source.
  Prefix is a filter only. It is not copied into the JSON.
  `lsp_ok` wraps the catalog. `lsp_emit` writes that reply.

  A hostile URI that is refused still returns the catalog when the
  prefix is empty. That catalog is public. It is not file bytes.

  Hover `Err(m) => m` can put an error string in hover source.
  Completion uses `Err(m) => ""`. That leak is not on this path.

## 5. Residual (not this fail)

  Hover is loose. Plan said refuse absolute paths outside the
  worktree when hover is loose.

  `file:///etc/passwd` has no `..`. The .oo gate allows the read.
  Runtime `oo_read_file` has no `OODA_FS_READDIR` jail.
  A symlink whose URI has no `..` can still follow.

  A naive "refuse every `/`" break would hit VS Code `file:///`
  URIs inside the tree. Empty source then yields the full catalog.
  That is a prefix bug, not a body print.

  Wave 3 brief: fix cli/lsp_complete.oo only if `..` is not refused.
  `..` is refused. SEC did not edit the product.

